    "rich_text_xbFPbM": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_ynjcCq": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>Why Peanut Butter Is Good for Dogs</strong>",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_faVBT6": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Peanut butter offers several health benefits for dogs, making it an excellent addition to their diet. Here’s why peanut butter is such a great choice for your dog:<br/><br/><strong>●Protein Power: </strong>Peanut butter is rich in protein, which helps with muscle growth and repair. Dogs need protein for overall health, and adding peanut butter to their treats is a great way to provide them with additional protein.<br/><br/><strong>●Healthy Fats:</strong> The healthy fats found in peanut butter give dogs long-lasting energy and help maintain a shiny, soft coat. These fats are also beneficial for your dog’s skin health.<br/><br/><strong>●Vitamins and Minerals:</strong> Peanut butter contains essential vitamins like B vitamins, vitamin E, and niacin. These nutrients help support your dog’s immune system, energy levels, and overall health.<br/><br/><strong>●Brain Health:</strong> The omega-3 and omega-6 fatty acids in peanut butter can enhance brain function, especially for senior dogs. These healthy fats play a critical role in maintaining cognitive function, which helps keep dogs sharp as they age.<br/><br/>When you feed your dog Snarky Pets’ Crunchy Peanut Butter Dog Treats, you're providing them with all the nutritional benefits of peanut butter in a fun, crunchy treat.<br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
