    "rich_text_7GJRRB": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_Q6cWLY": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>Peanut Butter and Dog Health: What to Consider</strong>",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_faMV36": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Peanut butter offers excellent health benefits, but it’s important to consider a few things when incorporating it into your dog’s diet:<br/><br/><strong>●Portion Control:</strong> Peanut butter is calorie-dense, so moderation is key. Treats like Crunchy Peanut Butter Dog Treats should make up no more than 10% of your dog’s daily caloric intake to avoid weight gain.<br/><br/><strong>●Dog Allergies:</strong> Some dogs may have peanut allergies. If your dog has an allergy to peanuts, look for alternative treats made from ingredients like sweet potato, coconut oil, or pumpkin.<br/><br/><strong>●Choosing the Right Peanut Butter: </strong>Always select natural peanut butter for your dog’s treats, avoiding products with added sugars, salt, or artificial sweeteners like xylitol. Snarky Pets ensures their treats are made with only the finest, dog-safe ingredients.<br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
